# MAVLY — Complete Website-Wide UI Consistency, Neumorphism & Motion Transformation

## PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Transform the existing Mavly application into a cohesive, polished, premium-quality product experience.

The current website has inconsistent UI components, slightly different colours and visual styles across sections, inconsistent buttons, awkward component designs, and missing page-entry and interaction animations.

Your task is to systematically audit and improve the entire existing frontend so that every page, section, component, button, and interaction follows one consistent design system.

This is a website-wide frontend refinement, not a backend rewrite or a new application.

The desired result should feel carefully engineered, visually cohesive, responsive, accessible, tactile, and premium.

**Do not merely add a few hover effects. Inspect the complete application, identify inconsistencies, implement a reusable design and motion system, apply it throughout the frontend, and verify the actual results.**

# NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES

## 1. 🎨 Colour inspection first

Before changing any colour, inspect the existing project's actual colour palette, CSS variables, theme configuration, shared components, global styles, and typography.

Do not prescribe or invent a new colour palette.

Do not blindly introduce a new theme, arbitrary gradients, unrelated accent colours, or hardcoded colour values.

Use the existing Mavly design system consistently throughout the entire application.

If the project supports multiple themes, preserve them and ensure all changes work correctly across the supported themes.

If additional design tokens are genuinely required, derive them from the existing system instead of introducing an unrelated visual identity.

## 2. ✨ Neumorphism / Soft UI

Use the existing design system's colours to create a refined Neumorphic / Soft UI experience.

Use subtle, controlled effects such as:

- Soft dual-light and dual-dark shadows.
- Gently elevated cards and surfaces.
- Tactile, extruded buttons.
- Pressed or inset interaction states.
- Subtle depth between related interface layers.
- Consistent borders and corner radii.
- Smooth, natural transitions between interaction states.

The result must look premium and intentional, not like every element has been given an exaggerated shadow.

Maintain readability, clear control boundaries, sufficient contrast, and accessibility.

Do not apply the same heavy shadow treatment to every element. Use elevation according to each component's purpose.

## 3. 🔒 Strict frontend-only scope

**Do not modify the backend, API routes, server logic, database, authentication configuration, environment variables, integrations, or business logic.**

Only make changes necessary to improve the existing frontend presentation, frontend interactions, animations, component styling, and routing transitions where supported.

Preserve every existing application capability and its underlying implementation.

Do not replace the existing application with a new template.

