# PHASE 5 — PREMIUM NEUMORPHISM WITHOUT OVERDESIGN

Apply the existing theme's Soft UI / Neumorphic visual language consistently where it makes sense.

## Buttons

Use subtle depth in normal states, an appropriate elevated hover state, and a tactile pressed state.

## Cards and panels

Use consistent shadows, neutral surfaces, and clear boundaries.

Avoid giving every card an identical exaggerated shadow or making unrelated cards appear physically raised for no reason.

## Inputs and form controls

Use restrained inset or raised surfaces where appropriate.

Preserve clear borders, labels, validation messages, and focus indicators.

## Menus, dropdowns, and modals

Use suitable elevation to separate floating components from the page.

Do not let the shadows obscure text or create unnecessary contrast problems.

## Navigation

Keep navigation items consistent, with clear active, hover, focus, and expanded states.

Avoid applying card-like shadows to every navigation link.

## Overall treatment

Use depth to establish hierarchy, not to decorate everything.

Do not create a plastic-looking UI with excessive highlights, dark borders, stacked shadows, or deep inset effects.

Maintain clear contrast and sufficient visual separation.

The result must look premium because the system is coherent, not because every component has a visible effect.

