# PHASE 9 — RESPONSIVENESS ACROSS ALL PAGES

Inspect every existing page across representative desktop, tablet, and mobile viewports.

Use the existing responsive breakpoints where possible.

Test representative widths around:

- 360px.
- 390px.
- 768px.
- 1024px.
- 1440px.

These are test targets, not a requirement to hardcode the entire design to exact pixel widths.

Verify:

- Navigation remains functional.
- Buttons remain accessible and appropriately sized.
- Cards and panels fit the screen.
- Typography wraps naturally.
- Forms remain usable.
- Dropdowns and modals stay within the viewport.
- Section animations do not cause overflow.
- Page transitions do not flash or reveal broken layouts.
- Touch interactions do not depend on hover.
- Responsive controls retain the correct active states.

Do not simply scale down desktop styles. Preserve the purpose and hierarchy of each page on smaller screens.

