# PHASE 11 — PERFORMANCE AND MAINTAINABILITY

The entire transformation must remain lightweight.

Prefer:

- CSS transitions for simple state changes.
- CSS transforms and opacity for motion.
- Existing animation libraries already installed in the project.
- Reusable component variants.
- Shared design tokens.
- Small, predictable frontend state transitions.

Avoid:

- Installing multiple animation libraries.
- Animating expensive layout properties unnecessarily.
- Constant JavaScript loops for simple animations.
- Repeatedly measuring the layout during animation.
- Excessive blur, filter, or shadow animations.
- Duplicate global CSS rules.
- Overly complicated animation abstractions.
- Rewriting the application structure unnecessarily.

Do not allow animation to degrade scrolling, input responsiveness, or the performance of the existing builder and editor.

Keep new code readable, component-focused, and compatible with the existing coding conventions.

