# PHASE 13 — COMPREHENSIVE TESTING AND VERIFICATION

Do not declare the transformation complete just because the frontend compiles.

Inspect the actual rendered application.

## 1. Route-by-route visual audit

Open every discovered route and verify its main sections and shared components.

Check for:

- Consistent theme and typography.
- Correct button variants.
- Standardised surface treatments.
- Appropriate page and section entrances.
- Consistent hover, focus, and pressed states.
- Proper spacing and alignment.
- No broken animations.
- No missing styles.
- No regressions in unique page layouts.

Do not inspect only `/home` and assume every other page inherits the correct design.

## 2. Interaction audit

Test every visible interactive control that is part of the scope.

Verify:

- Buttons respond to hover and press.
- Links navigate to their correct destinations.
- Dropdowns open and close.
- Accordions expand and collapse.
- Modals open and dismiss correctly.
- Inputs and selects remain usable.
- Tabs switch correctly.
- Forms preserve their real submission behaviour.
- Existing authentication buttons continue to work.
- Loading and disabled states remain accurate.
- Rapid interactions do not leave controls stuck.
- Animation never prevents the actual action.

Use automated browser tests or existing UI-testing tools where available. Otherwise, perform a systematic manual audit of the available pages and controls.

Do not claim that every button has been tested unless it has actually been tested.

## 3. Responsive audit

Check the main pages and shared components at desktop, tablet, and mobile widths.

Confirm that animations do not cause layout shifts, clipping, horizontal overflow, or inaccessible controls.

## 4. Accessibility audit

Check keyboard navigation, visible focus, reduced-motion behaviour, and readable contrast.

Run available accessibility checks where appropriate.

## 5. Technical checks

Run the relevant existing checks supported by the repository:

- Type checking.
- Linting.
- Production build.
- Existing frontend tests.
- Relevant browser or visual tests.

Fix issues introduced by the transformation.

Do not bypass existing checks simply to obtain a green result.

Do not claim a test has passed unless it was actually executed.

## 6. Final diff audit

Before finishing, inspect the changed files.

Confirm that:

- Changes are limited to the intended frontend work.
- No backend or server files were modified.
- No environment configuration was changed.
- No authentication implementation was altered.
- No integration or business logic was touched.
- No unrelated routes were removed or changed.
- No unnecessary dependencies were introduced.

If an existing project limitation prevents complete verification, report it accurately.

